// Course content: modules, extra questions, practicals, glossary, diagrams
const D1='<svg viewBox="0 0 300 150" role="img" aria-label="Forklift stability triangle seen from above"><polygon points="40,30 40,120 250,75" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/><circle cx="40" cy="30" r="7" fill="#F2B705" stroke="#1B2430"/><circle cx="40" cy="120" r="7" fill="#F2B705" stroke="#1B2430"/><circle cx="250" cy="75" r="7" fill="#F2B705" stroke="#1B2430"/><circle cx="120" cy="75" r="6" fill="#1F7A45"/><circle cx="22" cy="75" r="6" fill="#C93A0E"/><text x="52" y="22">front wheels</text><text x="200" y="100">rear pivot</text><text x="104" y="62">safe</text><text x="8" y="98">tips</text><text x="8" y="144">Centre of gravity must stay inside the triangle</text></svg>';
const D2='<svg viewBox="0 0 300 130" role="img" aria-label="Snatch block doubles winch pull"><line x1="0" y1="110" x2="300" y2="110" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="14" y="62" width="70" height="38" fill="#F2B705" stroke="#1B2430" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="30" cy="104" r="7"/><circle cx="68" cy="104" r="7"/><line x1="84" y1="72" x2="236" y2="72" stroke="#C93A0E" stroke-width="3"/><line x1="84" y1="88" x2="236" y2="82" stroke="#C93A0E" stroke-width="3"/><circle cx="246" cy="77" r="10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="262" y="30" width="12" height="80" fill="currentColor"/><text x="90" y="56">winch line out and back</text><text x="196" y="26">anchor</text><text x="8" y="126">Two lines: about double the pull, half the strain</text></svg>';
const M=[
{t:"1. Trade introduction and safety",n:["A recovery mechanic gets stuck, broken-down or crashed vehicles moving or safely off the road.","Work happens at night, in rain, mud and beside live traffic. Plan before you touch anything.","Assess first: people, fire or fuel risk, traffic, ground, vehicle weight and damage. Then choose the method.","Never stand in line with a loaded rope, chain or strap. They can snap and whip back.","Wear hi-vis, gloves, safety boots and eye protection every time."],q:[["What comes first at a recovery scene?",["Hook up the vehicle","Assess people, hazards and traffic","Start the winch","Take photos"],1],["Where should you never stand?",["Beside the truck","Behind a barrier","In line with a loaded rope or chain","Near the cab"],2]]},
{t:"2. Tools, equipment and PPE",n:["Core gear: jack and stands, wheel brace, jump pack, tow bar, chains, straps, shackles, snatch blocks, dollies, lights and triangles.","Every item has a working load limit (WLL). It is well below the breaking strength. Never exceed it.","Inspect before use. Reject frayed rope, cracked links, bent hooks and damaged stitching.","Store straps and ropes clean, dry and out of sunlight."],q:[["What is the WLL?",["The most the item can safely carry in use","Its weight","Its breaking point","Its price class"],0],["A strap with cuts and fraying should be:",["Used lightly","Knotted","Taken out of service","Washed"],2]]},
{t:"3. Roadside diagnosis and quick fixes",n:["Ask the driver what happened, what they heard and saw, and what warning lights came on.","No start: check battery terminals, battery charge, fuel level, fuses and the starter signal.","Overheating: stop, let it cool, never open a hot radiator cap. Check coolant, hoses and belt.","Jump start: red to dead +, red to donor +, black to donor -, last black clamp to bare metal on the dead car away from the battery.","If the fault is not fixable safely on site, tow."],q:[["Where does the last jump lead clamp go?",["Dead battery -","Bare metal away from the battery","Donor +","Fuse box"],1],["An overheated engine: you should",["Open the radiator cap at once","Pour cold water on it","Let it cool before opening the cap","Keep driving"],2]]},
{t:"4. Tyres, wheels and batteries on site",n:["Park on firm level ground, handbrake on, wheels chocked, hazards on.","Loosen nuts a little before jacking. Lift only at the jacking points. Never work under a car held by a jack alone.","Tighten nuts in a star pattern, then re-check torque after a short drive.","A battery that keeps going flat points to a charging fault or a drain. Test before replacing."],q:[["Wheel nuts are tightened:",["Clockwise in a circle","In a star pattern","One only","Fully before lifting"],1],["Work under a vehicle supported by:",["A jack only","A stand or secure support","A brick","Nothing"],1]]},
{t:"5. Towing methods and vehicle types",n:["Flatbed: best for all-wheel-drive, low, damaged or valuable cars.","Wheel-lift: lift the driven wheels. Front-wheel-drive is lifted at the front.","Rear-wheel-drive automatics: lift the rear, use dollies, or remove the propshaft. Towing on the drive wheels can damage the gearbox.","Check steering lock, handbrake, lights and tow-bar rating before moving.","Keep speed low and allow longer braking distance."],q:[["Best method for an all-wheel-drive car:",["Hook and chain","Flatbed","Rope","Push"],1],["Towing a front-wheel-drive car on a wheel-lift, lift the:",["Rear wheels","Front wheels","Neither","Roof"],1]]},
{t:"6. Winching and rigging",n:["Find a solid anchor: tree base, heavy vehicle or ground anchor. Protect trees with a wide strap.","Use shackles rated above the load. Pins fully seated, then back a quarter turn.","Lay a heavy cloth or damper over the middle of the rope to reduce whip if it breaks.","A snatch block gives two lines and about double the pull. Winch strain halves.","Pull straight where possible. Angled pulls load parts unevenly. Keep everyone clear."],q:[["A snatch block does what?",["Cuts the rope","Doubles the pull and halves winch strain","Weighs down the load","Stops the winch"],1],["Why drape a damper on the rope?",["Decoration","Reduces whip if the rope fails","Cools the rope","Marks the rope"],1]],s:D2},
{t:"7. Accident and heavy vehicle recovery",n:["Police, fire and medical needs come before recovery. Do not move a scene until it is released.","Isolate the battery and watch for leaking fuel, airbags not yet fired and damaged high-voltage parts.","Overturned trucks: unload first if allowed, then plan an upright with two lines and a controlled roll.","Damaged steering or brakes mean the vehicle must be carried or fully lifted, not towed on its wheels.","Photograph the scene and damage before moving anything."],q:[["Before moving an accident vehicle:",["Move it fast","Get clearance and photograph the scene","Ignore the police","Start the engine"],1],["Vehicle has broken steering. You should:",["Tow it on its wheels","Carry or fully lift it","Push it","Drive it slowly"],1]]},
{t:"8. Heavy equipment and plant: forklift module",n:["Types: counterbalance, reach truck, pallet jack. Know the load plate and rated capacity.","Stability triangle: two front wheels and the rear axle pivot form a triangle. The combined centre of gravity must stay inside it.","Raised, forward or side-loaded weight pushes the centre outside the triangle and tips the machine.","If it tips: stay belted and in the seat, hold on, lean away from the fall. Do not jump.","Servicing: check mast, chains, forks, hydraulic hoses, tyres, brakes and battery or fuel before each shift.","Recovering a tipped forklift: isolate power, spill control, then lift or roll upright with rated slings."],q:[["If a forklift starts to tip, you should:",["Jump out","Stay belted and brace","Raise the forks","Brake hard sideways"],1],["Stability depends on the centre of gravity staying:",["Above the mast","Inside the stability triangle","At the front","Outside the wheels"],1]],s:D1},
{t:"9. Scene management and traffic safety",n:["Place warning triangles and lights early enough to give approaching drivers time to slow. Go further on fast roads and bends.","Park the recovery truck to shield the work area, with lights on.","Work on the side away from traffic where possible.","Keep bystanders back and one person watching traffic."],q:[["Warning triangles should be placed:",["After the job","Early enough for drivers to slow down","Never","Behind the truck only"],1],["Best working side:",["Traffic side","Away from traffic","Middle of road","Any"],1]]},
{t:"10. Loading, documentation and customer handling",n:["Secure the vehicle with chains or straps at proper points. Check wheel nets and tie-downs again after a short distance.","Never exceed the truck’s load rating or axle limits.","Record the condition, photos, odometer, time and location before loading.","Explain price, destination and risks clearly. Get a signed handover."],q:[["Before loading you should:",["Skip records","Record condition and take photos","Hide damage","Ask nothing"],1],["Tie-downs should be re-checked:",["Never","After a short distance","Next week","Only at the yard"],1]]},
{t:"11. Business basics",n:["Price by distance, vehicle weight, hours, risk and equipment used. Keep a clear price list.","Dispatch: take caller name, number, exact location, vehicle, fault and number of people.","Keep insurance current for the truck, cargo and staff.","Maintain your own truck, winch and straps. A failed recovery truck costs jobs."],q:[["Most important detail to take from a caller:",["Their age","Exact location","Their job","Their car colour only"],1],["Why maintain your own equipment?",["Looks","A failure stops work and creates danger","No reason","Tax only"],1]]}
];
const X=[["Which PPE is needed on every job?",["Hi-vis, gloves, safety boots","Sandals","A suit","None if it is quick"],0],["How often should recovery gear be inspected?",["Yearly","Never","Before each use","When it breaks"],2],["A battery that goes flat again after charging suggests:",["Cold paint","A charging fault or drain","A wrong radio","A good battery"],1],["Before jacking a wheel you should:",["Remove the nuts fully","Lift at the bumper","Start the engine","Chock wheels and set the handbrake"],3],["Why check steering lock and handbrake before towing?",["So the car can steer and will not roll","For looks","Rules only","No reason"],0],["Shackle pins should be:",["Left loose","Fully seated then backed a quarter turn","Hammered in","Removed"],1],["Injured people, fire and fuel are dealt with:",["Before recovery","After recovery","Never","By the customer"],0],["A common forklift pre-shift check is:",["Radio","Paint","Mast, chains, forks and hydraulics","Seat colour"],2],["Who should watch traffic during the job?",["Nobody","The customer","Passers-by","One assigned person"],3],["Why get a signed handover?",["It proves condition and what was agreed","Paper only","For fun","Law forbids it"],0],["A dispatcher should confirm the:",["Weather elsewhere","Caller’s hobby","Truck colour","Vehicle, fault and exact location"],3]];
M.forEach((m,i)=>m.q.push(X[i]));
const P=[["Jump start a car",["Park cars close, engines and ignition off","Red clamp to dead battery +","Red clamp to donor +","Black clamp to donor -","Last black clamp to bare metal on the dead car, away from the battery","Start the donor, then the dead car","Remove clamps in reverse order"]],["Change a wheel on site",["Hazards on, firm level ground, handbrake, wheels chocked","Loosen nuts slightly","Jack at the jacking point","Remove nuts and wheel","Fit spare, hand-tighten nuts","Lower, then tighten in a star pattern","Re-check torque after a short drive"]],["Load a car on a flatbed",["Scene safe, bed tilted and aligned","Steering lock off, handbrake released","Attach winch to a rated recovery point","Winch slowly with a guide","Handbrake on, in gear or Park","Secure four points with straps or chains","Re-check tie-downs after a short distance"]],["Winch recovery with a snatch block",["Assess ground, load and anchor","Protect the anchor with a wide strap","Check rope, shackles and WLL","Rig the snatch block, pin seated","Drape a damper on the rope","Everyone clear of the line","Take up slack, pull steadily, stop to reassess"]],["Forklift pre-use check",["Seat belt, horn, lights and alarm work","Forks straight, no cracks","Mast and chains undamaged","Hydraulic hoses dry, no leaks","Tyres and wheels sound","Brakes and parking brake hold","Battery charge or fuel level OK"]],["Set up a roadside scene",["Park the truck to shield the work area, lights on","Place triangles early, further back on fast roads","Use cones to guide traffic","Assign one person to watch traffic","Keep bystanders back","Work on the side away from traffic"]]];
const G=[["WLL","Working load limit: the most an item is rated to carry in normal use."],["Breaking strength","The load at which an item fails. Well above the WLL."],["Snatch block","A pulley that redirects a winch line and doubles the pull."],["Shackle","A U-shaped link closed with a pin, used to join rigging."],["Recovery point","A rated attachment point on a vehicle for pulling or lashing."],["Flatbed","A truck with a tilting bed that carries the whole vehicle."],["Wheel-lift","A tow rig that lifts the driven wheels off the ground."],["Dollies","Small wheel frames that let you move a car with locked or driven wheels lifted."],["Propshaft","The shaft that carries drive from gearbox to rear axle."],["Damper","Heavy cloth draped on a rope to reduce whip if it breaks."],["Anchor point","A solid object that holds a winch or pull."],["Stability triangle","The three support points of a forklift. The centre of gravity must stay inside."],["Counterbalance","A forklift with rear weight that offsets the load on the forks."],["Load plate","The plate showing a forklift’s rated capacity."]];

