const sh=a=>a.map(x=>[Math.random(),x]).sort((p,q)=>p[0]-q[0]).map(x=>x[1]);
const qb=(k,t)=>{const m=M.find(m=>m.t.includes(k));t.trim().split('\n').forEach(l=>{const p=l.split('|'),o=sh(p.slice(1));m.q.push([p[0],o,o.indexOf(p[1])])})};
qb("Trade introduction",`What does a risk assessment aim to do?|Spot hazards and plan controls before work|Speed up the job|Replace PPE|Reduce paperwork
Who can call a stop on an unsafe job?|Anyone on site|Only the owner|Only the driver|Only the police
Fallen power lines should be treated as:|Live|Dead|Harmless if wet|Safe if lying on the ground
Which PPE matters most when handling wire rope?|Gloves|Sunglasses|Ear plugs|A scarf
Why avoid loose clothing near winch drums?|It can be caught and pull you in|It looks untidy|It gets dirty|It slows you down
Which number is Ghana’s fire service line?|192|191|193|100
Tiredness on the job should be treated as:|A safety hazard|A minor issue|A sign of hard work|Irrelevant`);
qb("Tools, equipment",`In a rigging chain, the weakest part:|Sets the safe limit|Does not matter|Is always the hook|Is the longest part
Which fault means a chain link should be rejected?|A stretched or twisted link|Surface dust|Dry paint|Cold links
Webbing slings are damaged by:|Cuts, burns, chemicals and sunlight|Dry air|Short storage|Light loads
A shackle with a bent pin should be:|Taken out of service|Straightened|Used for light loads|Painted
A hook with an opened throat should be:|Replaced|Bent back|Welded|Used carefully
Ropes and straps should be stored:|Clean, dry, away from sun and chemicals|On the road|In a damp box|Next to fuel
The rating tag shows:|The load limit|The price|The colour code only|The maker’s address only`);
qb("Roadside diagnosis",`A rested 12 V battery should read about:|12.6 V|8 V|16 V|20 V
A clicking sound and no crank suggests:|A weak battery or starter solenoid|Empty washer fluid|Bad wipers|A loose mirror
No lights and no crank suggests:|A dead battery or disconnected terminals|A blocked exhaust|Worn tyres|A dirty air filter
The radiator cap should be opened:|Only when the engine is cold|When hot|While running|Never check coolant
A red oil warning light means:|Stop the engine|Drive on|Add air|Ignore it until home
A diesel cranks but will not start. Check:|Fuel filter and air in the lines|Tyre pressure|Wiper blades|The mirrors
Which fault means tow, not repair on site?|Brake failure|Low washer fluid|A dim dash light|A dirty windscreen`);
qb("Tyres, wheels",`Wheel nuts are loosened before lifting by about:|Half a turn|Fully|Not at all|Ten turns
Wheel nut torque should be re-checked after about:|50 km|1000 km|A year|Never
Tyre plugs and patches are suitable for:|The tread area only|Sidewalls|Any damage|Bulges
When disconnecting a battery, remove first:|The negative|The positive|Both together|Neither
Before a roadside wheel change, the spare should be:|Checked for pressure and condition|Painted|Ignored|Left flat
Battery gases are:|Explosive|Harmless|Cooling|Non-flammable
Never jump a battery that is:|Cracked or frozen|Cold at night|Slightly dusty|Warm`);
qb("Towing methods",`A flatbed suits:|All-wheel-drive, low and damaged vehicles|Only trucks|Only scooters|Nothing
A rear-wheel-drive automatic on a wheel-lift is best:|Lifted at the rear or on dollies|Lifted at the front only|Towed on drive wheels far|Pushed
The steering lock must be:|Released before towing|Locked|Ignored|Welded
Towing with the engine off needs:|Longer braking distance|Shorter braking distance|No change|Higher speed
Locked or seized wheels are best moved with:|Dollies or a flatbed|A tow rope|Pushing|A jack
Slide-on ramps help with:|Low cars|Tall trucks|Tyre fitting|Painting
Before towing, check:|Tow bar rating and lights|The radio station|The seat colour|The paint`);
qb("Winching",`Winch pull is highest on:|A bare drum|A full drum|The last layer|Every layer equally
Minimum turns of rope to keep on the drum:|Five|One|None|Twenty
Side pulls can:|Stack rope on one side and damage the winch|Improve the pull|Cool the winch|Do nothing
A steel wire rope hazard is:|Sharp broken strands|It floats|It stretches like rubber|It never wears
A synthetic rope advantage is:|Light and safer if it snaps|Unbreakable|Heat proof|Needs no inspection
Never use a winch for:|Towing over a long distance|Short pulls|Recoveries|Light pulls
Anchor trees should be protected with:|A wide strap|Bare chain|Wire rope|Nothing`);
qb("Off-road",`In soft sand, lower tyre pressure helps by:|Widening the footprint|Raising the car|Cooling tyres|Adding speed
Carry a compressor to:|Re-inflate tyres afterwards|Cool the engine|Charge the battery|Pump fuel
A kinetic rope rating should be:|Well above the stuck vehicle’s weight|Below the weight|Unimportant|Chosen by colour
Water above the air intake can cause:|Hydro-lock|Better cooling|Higher power|Nothing
After a water crossing, check:|Brakes and the oil for a milky look|The radio|Seat belts only|Window tint
A bow shackle beats a hook because it:|Takes loads from several angles|Is cheaper|Is lighter|Looks better
The best recovery pull direction is usually:|Back along the way the vehicle came|Sideways|Uphill always|Across the slope`);
qb("Accident and heavy",`Who controls the scene on arrival?|The police or incident commander|The tow driver|Bystanders|The customer
Hybrid high-voltage cables are usually coloured:|Orange|Green|Blue|Yellow
To upright a truck, attach lines to:|Chassis and axles|The cab roof|Body panels|Mirrors
The second line when uprighting:|Prevents it slamming down|Pulls harder|Is decoration|Marks the zone
Fuel spills should be:|Soaked up with absorbent|Washed into drains|Left alone|Set alight
Pulling along an embankment slope helps:|Keep the vehicle from rolling|Save time|Cut fuel|Look neat
Air-brake spring brakes apply when:|Air is lost|Air is supplied|The engine is hot|The truck is clean`);
qb("forklift",`The stability triangle has:|Three support points|Two|Five|Six
Travel with forks:|Low and the mast tilted back|Raised|Level and high|Sideways
A load plate shows:|Rated capacity at a stated load centre|Fuel type|Age|Colour
Never allow anyone to:|Ride on the forks|Walk near the truck|Wear hi-vis|Use the horn
Lead-acid charging gives off:|Explosive hydrogen|Oxygen only|Nothing|Cold air
LPG cylinders should be stored:|Upright and outdoors|On their side indoors|Near heat|In the cab
Lift a tipped forklift by slinging from:|The overhead guard or chassis points|The mast|The forks only|The seat`);
qb("Scene management",`The recovery truck is placed to:|Shield the work area|Block ambulances|Look neat|Save fuel
A taper of cones:|Moves traffic over gradually|Stops all traffic|Marks parking|Marks fuel
The traffic watcher:|Watches traffic and warns the team|Drives the truck|Collects payment|Takes photos
Bystanders should stay back at least:|1.5 times the line length|Half the line length|One metre|No distance
In rain, warning triangles go:|Further back|Closer|Behind the car|Away from the road
Hand signals should be agreed:|Before work starts|After the pull|Never|Only at night
Work on the side:|Away from traffic|Beside traffic|In the middle|Facing traffic`);
qb("Loading, documentation",`Minimum tie-down points on a car:|Four|One|Two|None
Tie-downs are best attached to:|Rated points or the wheels|Suspension arms|The exhaust|Mirrors
Photograph the vehicle:|On all sides before and after|Only after|Never|Only the plate
Before moving a vehicle, get the customer’s:|Consent and signature|Opinion on the weather|Shoe size|Favourite colour
Keys and valuables should be:|Recorded on the job card|Ignored|Taken home|Left in the car
The strap angle that holds best is about:|45 degrees|Flat|Vertical|Random
Re-check tie-downs:|After a short distance and at stops|Never|Once a week|Only at the yard`);
qb("Business basics",`A call-out fee covers:|Getting the truck to the job|Parts only|Tax only|Nothing
Quoting before work helps:|Avoid disputes|Reduce pay|Hide costs|Skip invoices
Truck insurance should also include:|Public liability|Nothing|Only fuel|Only tyres
Job records are kept for:|Each truck and each job|No one|Only the client|Only the police
Dispatch should log:|Time, caller, location, vehicle and fault|Only the name|Only the price|Nothing
If arrival is delayed:|Update the caller|Switch off the phone|Cancel silently|Ignore it
Build links with:|Garages, insurers, haulage firms and police|No one|Only friends|Competitors only`);

